@strong{Edition notes.} The compiler is implemented in
@code{ocaml/@/examples/@/ch5/@/sec_5_5.ml}.  The public interface
@code{Sec_5_5.compile} accepts an AST expression.
@code{Sec_5_5.compile_program} compiles top-level items, and
@code{Sec_5_5.load} assembles the typed sequence.
@code{Sec_5_5.run} executes a checked program;
@code{Sec_5_5.run_stats} also reports executed instructions.
@code{Sec_5_5.statements_text} renders statements for inspection.

The AST is defined in @code{ocaml/@/common/@/ast.ml}.  It uses
@code{Scalar}, @code{Var}, @code{Let}, @code{Fun}, @code{Apply},
@code{If}, @code{Match}, and the other variants described above.
References use @code{Make_ref}, @code{Deref}, and @code{Assign};
there are no quote, variable-set, or conditional-derived-form nodes.
The compiler's state generates labels.  Its compiled closures retain an
entry label, parameter names, and their captured environment.

@code{Metacircular.evaluator} is the guest evaluator source.
@code{Metacircular.with_guest} returns a complete unit containing that
evaluator, one guest expression, and a printing driver.  The current
compiler interface does not provide a combined driver-loop coordinator.
Exercises 5.47 through 5.52 describe extensions or backends, not current
compiler entry points.
